---
description: Atlas OS architecture and domain conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Use a modular Next.js monolith. Keep domain logic in `src/domain` and `src/server`, not in React components.

Required boundaries:

- Auth/session validation in a server-only DAL
- Atlas runtime (context assembly, model routing, tools, streaming)
- Memory as structured records with provenance and invalidation
- Capabilities as a registry that future Operatives can join

Do not add LangChain, LangGraph, Mem0, Zep, Letta, a dedicated vector database, a graph database, or microservices.

Every query for owner data must be scoped by the authenticated `userId`.

AI providers are adapters. Atlas identity lives in constitution, context, memory, and tools.

See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/DATA-MODEL.md`.
